<title>USA: High pressure continues hold on Brazil coffee- WSC.</title>
<headline>High pressure continues hold on Brazil coffee- WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The warm ridge of high pressure holding over Brazil's coffee belt is expected to remain in the area while cold air passes off to the south over the weekend, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Clouds and a few light showers were reported in the coffee belt this morning. Low temperatures ranged from 54-59 F (12-15 C).</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies are expected through Thursday. Temperatures should remain near to above normal with lows in the 50's to low 60's F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>Partly to variably cloudy skies are expected for Friday with the chance of a few showers favoring the southern portion of the region. Temperatures should stay near normal levels with no damaging cold in the forecast, according to WSC.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
</text>
